<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Third Dynasty of Ur</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">2112–2004 BCE</span> · Also known as Ur III</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Third Dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ur">Ur</a>, also called Ur III or the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/neo-sumerian-empire">Neo-Sumerian Empire</a>, was a Mesopotamian state that ruled from the city of Ur from 2112 to 2004 BCE. Founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ur-nammu">Ur-Nammu</a>, it built a highly centralised bureaucratic administration on Akkadian precedents. It dominated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elam">Elam</a> until the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shimashki-dynasty">Shimashki</a> king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kindattu">Kindattu</a> sacked Ur around 2004 BCE, and its collapse allowed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assur">Assur</a> to emerge as an independent city-state.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/third-dynasty-of-ur.jpg" alt="Third Dynasty of Ur" width="320" height="245" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Middle_East_topographic_map-blank.svg: Sémhur (talk) derivative work: Zunkir (talk) · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ur_III.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
